  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Thursday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nSouth winds return tomorrow, with a corresponding return to near\nto just above normal temperatures for the afternoon. Warmer and\nbreezier conditions are on deck for Saturday in advance of the\nnext cold front, which remains on track to move through Saturday\nnight into early Sunday. Moisture increasing ahead of the front in\nresponse to an increasing low level jet will lead to rain chances\nacross parts of northeast Oklahoma and western Arkansas early\nSunday morning, with wraparound moisture keeping low chances\naround in mainly far northeast Oklahoma and far northwest Arkansas\nthrough midday Sunday. Will need to keep an eye on temperature\nprofile trends with the wraparound moisture precipitation for\npotential rain/snow mix before moving out. Behind this cold front,\nnorth to northwesterly winds will be gusty, featuring gusts in \nthe 30 to 40 mph range into Sunday afternoon. \n\nSurface high pressure behind the weekend cold front will move\nthrough Sunday night, leading to another chilly morning Monday,\nfollowed by returning southerly winds and near normal temperatures\nfor Monday afternoon. A steady warmup looks continue through the\nmiddle of the week, with a fast-moving storm system Tuesday \nlikely to have little impact.\n\nLate next week yet another storm system will approach the region,\nwith increasing southerly winds ahead of it. Given its track and a\nmore prolonged period of moisture return, rain chances will return\nThursday into Friday.",
